From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:29:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: Clear the QoS Map with an empty SET_QOS_MAP_SET

SET_QOS_MAP_SET sets the QoS Map of the driver and the configured one
of a running BSS. It refuses a map of fewer than 16 values, so no
control interface command removes the QoS Map from a running BSS.

Let an empty SET_QOS_MAP_SET clear the QoS Map of the driver and the
configured one. cfg80211 clears the map for an NL80211_CMD_SET_QOS_MAP
without NL80211_ATTR_QOS_MAP, so nl80211_set_qos_map() leaves the
attribute out for an empty map. The nl80211 policy rejects an attribute
of fewer than 16 octets.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/hostapd/ctrl_iface.c
+++ b/hostapd/ctrl_iface.c
@@ -659,6 +659,16 @@ static int hostapd_ctrl_iface_set_qos_ma
 	const char *pos = cmd;
 	int val, ret;
 
+	if (!*cmd) {
+		if (hostapd_drv_set_qos_map(hapd, NULL, 0)) {
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "Failed to clear QoS Map Set");
+			return -1;
+		}
+
+		hapd->conf->qos_map_set_len = 0;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	for (;;) {
 		if (count == sizeof(qos_map_set)) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "Too many qos_map_set parameters");
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -12893,8 +12893,10 @@ static int nl80211_set_qos_map(void *pri
 	wpa_hexdump(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Setting QoS Map",
 		    qos_map_set, qos_map_set_len);
 
+	/* cfg80211 clears the map of a request without NL80211_ATTR_QOS_MAP */
 	if (!(msg = nl80211_cmd_msg(bss, 0, NL80211_CMD_SET_QOS_MAP)) ||
-	    nla_put(msg, NL80211_ATTR_QOS_MAP, qos_map_set_len, qos_map_set)) {
+	    (qos_map_set_len &&
+	     nla_put(msg, NL80211_ATTR_QOS_MAP, qos_map_set_len, qos_map_set))) {
 		nlmsg_free(msg);
 		return -ENOBUFS;
 	}
